{
  "$comment": "THE BUS (lib/sessions/bus.ts, trpc sessions.reply/report, lib/integrations/pr-sync.ts). Every transition of a session S is posted into its LISTENERS: its parent (whatever its status), then every LIVE session whose wakeOn names S, by id, each once. A line authored BY S (`authorSessionId` = S) and WAKING is pending input for its reader (the reader's device delivers it: that is the wake-up); a reader that has ended keeps the row, not waking. With no listener at all an event line lands on S itself, not waking (`session_claimed` excepted: it never falls back). WHAT WAKES: S's turn reply (agent-authored; a watching team agent conversation that is not S's parent hears no turns), S's question/plan (an `ask` mirror card naming the card row; askText, or the neutral askHidden line), S's wall (`session_blocked`, once: only when S was not blocked and the device does not handle it), S's PR (`pr_opened`, with the PR id), S's END (a `report` card: the summary, else S's last plain reply, else rules.report.fallback, clipped to report.max; a sealed summary or reply is never read). After its report nobody watches S (it leaves every wakeOn). Silent events (rules.assistantSilentEvents) skip an Assistant's conversation. PRIVACY: a listener whose readers may not see S (S private and the listener shared, or another member's) gets a NEUTRAL line for a reply, a report, a PR and an ask (copy.private* / askHidden). SEALED (EXP-1458): a sealed reply reaches listeners in S's own tree as a byte copy, listeners in another tree as the copy the device sealed for that tree (`copies[rootId]`), else the neutral line. A blank reply with no card is refused.",
